<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Dec 21.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Dec 21.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended December 21</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   230	   0.77     304900  70.13    17.46</p>
<p>Reliance	     205	   0.36     230000  47.15     9.16</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   166	   0.59     277200  46.02    18.53</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    225	   0.61     110950  24.96    14.14</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    340	   1.11	67650  23.00    17.02</p>
<p>Tata Power	   121	   0.47     185650  22.46    20.25</p>
<p>MTNL		   235	   0.59	86700  20.37    13.09</p>
<p>Hind Lever	   820	   0.32	18500  15.17     2.03</p>
<p>IPCL		   121	   0.17	62400   7.55     7.33</p>
<p>Bhel		   225	   0.83	33500   7.54    19.23</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 15.71 percent on an annualised basis against 5.18 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Dec 14.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
